    "name": "Swipe cards — Decipher",
    "description": "A native three-column radio matrix enhanced as accessible swipe cards. Synthetic demo; variable plain-text rows.",
    "platform": "decipher",
    "instructions": "Use SwipeCards for a requested swipe-card single-select matrix. Supply label, title, instructions, and an array of rows with label/text. Keep column labels c1/c2/c3 and export values 1/2/3 fixed: Dislike/Skip/Like. Never turn Skip into missing. After the last choice, preserve the bundled guarded completion through the actual native Continue button. Use one to twenty rows with unique valid Decipher labels. Use plain text only. Preserve native radio inputs and scoped bundled styles. Do not add shuffle, exclusive rows, open-ended cells, row conditions, or other interactive styles without a separate native verification. Put the rendered component in main, followed by a suspend. Generate no extra substantive questions for a single-question request. Keep only the question, cards and Dislike/Skip/Like controls visible. No review page, Back, Undo, card navigation, fallback toggle, debug display, progress labels or teaching copy. Disable native Back with ss:enableNavigation=\"0\". Preserve accessible instructions. Hide native Continue only after successful enhancement; restore it and the matrix on validation/re-entry or after a stalled request. Finish the final animation, remove the deck, and invoke the existing native Continue button once when every row is selected. Never bypass native validation with form.submit or introduce repeated automatic retries. Use only one question per page. Keep the bundled pointer tracking, edge fade, directional cue, threshold snap-back, locked single-commit animation and subtle next-card preview; buttons use the same transition. Respect reduced motion and vertical scrolling. Verify native required validation and output mapping after generation.",
    "skeleton_source": "<survey name=\"Weekend ideas\" alt=\"Weekend ideas\" compat=\"144\" fir=\"on\" html:showNumber=\"0\" builder:wizardCompleted=\"1\" state=\"testing\" ss:enableNavigation=\"0\" extraVariables=\"source\">\n{{slot:main}}<suspend/>\n\n</survey>\n",
    "slots": [
      {
        "id": "main",
        "name": "Main questions",
        "description": "Place the SwipeCards component here."
      }
    ],
